WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.268
Ukrainian soldiers are reuniting

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.069
with family

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.570
and friends

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.372
after the eight month

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.474
long Russian occupation.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.675
The people of Arizona Zone

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.642
are celebrating

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.810
the liberation of their cities,

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.046
singing patriotic songs and crying.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.615
Climbing to the tops of buildings

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.550
to hoist the Ukrainian flag.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.185
But her son is facing

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.687
challenging mandatory conditions.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.721
Large parts of the city

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.622
are without electricity

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.623
and running water.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.591
There are also reports

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:25.458
of landmines

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.393
and other hazards

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.328
left behind by Russian troops.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.295
But Zelinski says

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.830
efforts are now being made

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.199
to return the city to normalcy.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.402
Here's what he told the G-20 summit.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.536
That was earlier this morning.

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.039
Watch Vietnam.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:39.873
Pretty glad

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.708
It is like, for example, D-Day,

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.710
the landing of the allies in Normandy.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.477
It was not yet

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.479
a final point in the fight against evil,

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.048
but it already determined

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.550
the entire further course of events.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.685
If the victory will be ours in any case,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.187
and we are sure of it,

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:54.654
then shouldn't

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.823
we try to implement our formula for peace

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.658
to save thousands of lives

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.993
and protect the world from

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.394
further destabilization?

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.931
Zielinski also outlining a peace proposal

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.266
which includes the end

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.534
to nuclear threats,

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.769
more food and energy security,

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:10.637
prisoner swaps

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:13.173
and a full withdrawal by Russia.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.442
Is this the beginning

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:16.443
of the end of the war?

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.211
As President Zelensky says,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:18.912
let's discuss now.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:19.746
I want to bring in CNN's

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:20.780
chief international correspondent

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.082
Chris Award.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.017
Good morning to you there. How.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.785
How significant is Zelensky's

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:28.254
proposed peace plan to the G20

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.525
Well, I would have to say

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:36.196
it is obviously coming from a place of

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.997
buoyancy and exuberance

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.800
after the taking of Harrison

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.436
or the liberation of Hair Salon,

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.004
the demands are maximalist.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.940
There isn't a huge amount

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:47.807
in this ten point

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:48.408
peace plan

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.275
that the Russians

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.277
are likely to say, okay,

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.313
we have something we can start with here.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.648
So it's not

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.718
that the demands are sort of outlandish

00:01:58.718 --> 00:01:59.319
in any way.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.054
They really make a lot of sense,

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:01.921
and they pertain

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.090
to hugely important issues

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.191
that affect the whole world,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.327
like food security, energy security,

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:11.731
nuclear security, as well as demanding

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.399
that Russia withdraw its forces

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:13.867
and that there be

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.702
a cessation of hostilities.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.004
But in terms of how realist it is

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.006
to get the Russians

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.841
to come to the negotiating table

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.177
and use this as a starting draft,

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.679
that is probably more of a long shot

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:27.780
because the Russians

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.982
will obviously be wanting

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.184
to see more extractions

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.785
or at least some concessions

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.020
that they can take away.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.355
At this stage, though, guys,

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.990
I don't think that the Ukrainians

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.624
have any interest

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.492
in making those concessions. Right.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.861
And that's that's critical to all of this

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.264
as the winter comes. Right.

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.232
Which could completely change the game.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.400
And President Biden

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.201
is meeting with world

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.769
leaders at the G20,

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.071
hoping to really get them aligned.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.673
Can something significant

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.674
come out of the G20

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.476
that would really aid Ukraine at

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.077
this point in this, Clarissa?

00:02:59.279 --> 00:02:59.879
It's a really

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.481
tough one, Poppy, honestly,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.882
because at the end of the day,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.917
what you're hearing from U.S.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.552
officials, we've heard some in the U.S.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.053
military say, you know,

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.521
now's the time for Ukraine

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.890
to really take stock and sit down

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.126
and think about what a peace plan or what

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.794
some kind of a negotiated settlement

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.662
would look like.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.896
Other officials in the U.S.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.031
administration are saying

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.567
that's really not our place in the US

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:21.334
or in the White House

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.102
to be dictating to the Ukrainians

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.404
what the terms should look like

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.139
or when they should sit down

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.073
Ukraine right

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.341
now, understandably,

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.076
is not in the mood to negotiate.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.344
They've lost too much.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.845
They've just taken back her son.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.215
This is a huge strategic

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:35.949
and symbol

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.617
like humiliation for the Russians.

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.586
It was the only regional capital

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:41.821
and the largest city that they've taken

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.855
since the beginning

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.058
of the invasion back in February.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.526
At the same time,

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.427
while you have silenced

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.561
you talking about D-Day

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.729
and saying that it's clear

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.464
the trajectory of the war in the sense

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.199
that the Russians can't win.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.901
President Putin also understands

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.703
for his own political survival,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.971
he can't lose.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:58.471
And so what

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.473
the Russians are banking on at this stage

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.642
is that they can drag out

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.344
or protract this conflict

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.445
as long as they can

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.280
and make it as painful as they can.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.915
Not just for the Ukrainians,

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.717
but for the Western countries

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.318
that are backing Ukraine.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.586
And as you head into the winter,

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.121
as you head into a recession,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.790
they're hoping that that will sort of,

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:18.691
you know,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.826
push the Ukrainians,

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.527
that there will be more

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.763
sort of Ukraine supporters in the West

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.764
pushing them

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.332
to go to the negotiating table.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.600
But at this stage,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.702
I don't see that happening overnight.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:30.536
And of course,

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.239
we're also we're seeing such triumphant

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.175
voices, reaction coming out of her song

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.710
where it's been a long eight months

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.445
for these Ukrainians so far.

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.313
But we're also getting

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.181
a better picture of the torture

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.249
and the hell that they have been

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:44.384
living through

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:45.752
in this Russian occupation.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:47.954
That's right.

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:48.254
And it's

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:49.489
such an important thing,

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.189
I think, Caitlin,

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.425
to underscore for our viewers,

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.228
this is victory and victory

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.763
as you can see in those scenes of

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.364
jubilation is a beautiful thing.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.866
But it's also grim

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.701
because it is also now

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:02.435
the beginning

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.169
of the sort

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.103
of unpacking

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.605
of the trauma of the horrors

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.440
of what happened, of people

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.275
who were tortured, who were beaten.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.476
One man

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.645
allegedly for just spray painting,

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:13.946
you know, glory

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.215
be to Ukraine on a bus stop.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.583
So the people of Harrison,

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.252
many of them have lived through things

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.253
that are unthinkable

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.688
and they are now living in a city

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.989
that has had no electricity,

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.058
that probably won't have electricity

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.392
for several more months.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.394
And they're going into a winter

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:29.162
that promises

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:29.696
to be

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:30.596
brutally cold,

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.531
as the winter often

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:34.834
is under continued bombardment, strategic

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.135
targeting

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.470
of Ukraine's critical

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.272
civilian infrastructure.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:40.907
And so while this is a moment

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.642
for Ukraine to celebrate,

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.210
it is still painful

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.411
and there are still

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.612
many challenges ahead.

